      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="summary">
          <h2>1. Why edge financial applications fail in production</h2>
          <p>
            Commercial financial software — especially in multi-currency economies with flaky connectivity — routinely breaks due to five recurring engineering defects: storing money in floating-point (<code>double</code>), recomputing historical FX conversions dynamically, coupling physical cash register sessions with legal fiscal numbering, allowing mutable journal entries, and disbursing supplier payments without verifying goods receipt.
          </p>
          <p>
            This report documents the domain invariants implemented in <strong>Meson</strong> (<code>apps/meson_business</code>, <code>apps/meson_currency</code>, and <code>apps/meson_central</code>) to eliminate these five failure modes across runtime logic, persistence schemas, and automated tests.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="arithmetic">
          <h2>2. Exact integer cent math &amp; multi-currency FX snapshots</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Zero floating-point drift (<code>exact_cent_amounts.dart</code>):</strong> <code>ExactCentAmounts</code> models monetary amounts as exact integer cents bounded by the Dart/JavaScript safe integer ceiling (<code>maxExact = 9007199254740991</code>, 2<sup>53</sup>−1) and uses <code>BigInt</code> arithmetic for summations and range checks across JSON transport and ledger posting.</li>
            <li><strong>Immutable FX rate snapshots (<code>ExchangeRateService</code> &amp; <code>meson_currency</code>):</strong> every transaction freezes the exact exchange rate at execution time (<code>exchange_rate_model.dart</code>), guaranteeing that later FX shifts never mutate historical margins, Z-Closes, or ledger reports.</li>
            <li><strong>Dedicated currency conversion engine:</strong> <code>apps/meson_currency</code> (<code>currency_logic.dart</code>, <code>currency_rate_service.dart</code>) isolates fiat and digital denomination math into a reusable client.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="ledger">
          <h2>3. Double-entry ledger &amp; automated payment projection</h2>
          <div class="paper-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="en-fin-cap">
            <table class="paper-table">
              <caption id="en-fin-cap">Table 1 · Accounting modules and enforced invariants in <code>meson_business</code></caption>
