                  <th scope="row"><code>accounting_ledger_operations.dart</code></th>
                  <td data-label="Responsibility">Journal &amp; general ledger entries</td>
                  <td data-label="Invariant">Strict <code>∑ Debits == ∑ Credits</code> balance per entry in exact integer cents.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>accounting_posting_integrity.dart</code></th>
                  <td data-label="Responsibility">Immutability enforcement</td>
                  <td data-label="Invariant">Posted entries cannot be overwritten; corrections require auditable reversing entries.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>accounting_period_operations.dart</code></th>
                  <td data-label="Responsibility">Accounting period closure</td>
                  <td data-label="Invariant">Blocks retroactive postings into closed monthly or fiscal periods.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>payment_accounting_projector.dart</code></th>
                  <td data-label="Responsibility">POS-to-ledger projection</td>
                  <td data-label="Invariant">Maps split payments (cash, card, bank transfer, credit) into chart-of-accounts entries without duplication.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="fiscal">
          <h2>4. Cryptographic fiscal hash chain (SENIAT) &amp; issuer isolation</h2>
          <p>
            Following <code>FISCAL_ARCHITECTURE.md</code>, <code>FiscalAuditService</code>, <code>FiscalDocumentRepository</code>, and <code>FiscalIssuerRepository</code> enforce three regulatory invariants:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Register vs. fiscal decoupling:</strong> opening or closing a cash drawer never alters sequential fiscal numbering or document validity.</li>
            <li><strong>Sequential cryptographic hash chaining:</strong> each fiscal document incorporates the cryptographic hash of the immediately preceding document, creating a tamper-evident audit chain aligned with SENIAT requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Frozen issuer snapshots &amp; idempotent dispatch:</strong> tax issuer metadata is frozen per document, and retries verify idempotency before re-transmission.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="treasury">
          <h2>5. Blind Z-Close reconciliation, 3-Way AP matching &amp; SaaS MRR</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Blind cash-drawer count (<code>cash_checkout_totals.dart</code>):</strong> cashiers declare counted physical denominations without seeing expected totals; the controller reconciles opening float, drawer withdrawals (<code>cash_drawer_withdrawal_recorder</code>), card settlements, and variance before sealing Z-Close.</li>
            <li><strong>3-Way AP matching (<code>supplier_finance_integrity.dart</code>, <code>supplier_finance_safety.dart</code>):</strong> supplier disbursements (<code>supplier_payables_global.dart</code>) require cross-verification across Purchase Order ↔ Goods Received Note (GRN) ↔ Supplier Invoice.</li>
            <li><strong>Recursive BOM costing (<code>inventory_cost_evidence.dart</code>):</strong> real product costs roll up recursively across nested recipes adjusted by ingredient yield.</li>
            <li><strong>SaaS revenue &amp; cost plane (<code>meson_central</code>):</strong> <code>revenue_registry.dart</code> and <code>platform_costs_screen.dart</code> aggregate multi-tenant subscription MRR against cloud infrastructure spend.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="validity">
